 This appendix proves part~(iv) of Theorem~\ref{thm:free-coordinate}, the uniform-kernel sampler with its constant-arity trees, and shows that none of its constants depends on the class $c$ except through $c \le u$. Appendix~\ref{app:free-coordinate} proves parts~(i)--(iii) and reuses the tree, restart and error-split argument below for part~(ii). The second proof of Corollary~\ref{cor:fpt-r} given at the end of this appendix needs that uniformity, because there $c$ is not fixed. The proof uses the following results from the body of the paper: Theorem~\ref{thm:rees-cover} and Lemma~\ref{lem:homogeneous} (or Lemma~\ref{lem:copy-lift} for coset-copy input) for the lifted sources, Lemma~\ref{lem:central} (the branch law of the central instrument), Proposition~\ref{prop:descent} (pointwise quotient conversion), and the recursion of Section~\ref{sec:recursion} with its hybrid convention (Lemma~\ref{lem:hybrid}). It uses no other step of the paper, apart from the gate counts of Theorem~\ref{thm:uniform-compilation} in the cost bound of Section~\ref{app:s3-uniform}. Section~\ref{app:s3-mixed} also uses Theorem~\ref{thm:power-sde}, Remark~\ref{rem:is-import}(b), Theorem~\ref{thm:app-s2-main}, Remark~\ref{rem:combined-schedule} and Lemma~\ref{lem:fc-forest}.
 
