 \emph{Restarts.} Conditional on the records of all other trees, a tree acts on fresh registers with fresh coins, so it aborts with probability at most $1/32$. Hence fewer than $m'$ successes occur with probability at most $\binom{4m'}{3m'}32^{-3m'} \le 2^{-2m'} \le \eps/3$. From here the tree part of the proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:free-coordinate}(iv) above applies word for word, with $N_{\mathrm{instr}} \le 4m'\bigl(P + \sum_d n_d(M_d+1)\bigr) + m'$ complete instruments in place of~\eqref{eq:s3-ninstr}: the kept outputs are i.i.d.\ copies of $\rho_{H_1}$, the rank failure is at most $\eps/3$, and the implementation error is at most $\eps/3$. Each attempted tree has $P$ leaves of $c$ queries each. The trial count is Lemma~\ref{lem:s3-node}(e) with $M = M_d$.
 \end{proof}
 
